# Yuma AIA-A14: AI-speed exploitation burst - one client hitting many WAF rules across many paths in 10 minutes
# Source: AWS WAF logs in CloudWatch Logs. Fields as A13, plus ruleGroupList[].terminatingRule.ruleId (the managed
# rule inside a rule group; terminatingRuleId alone only names the group).
#   https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/logging-fields.html
# Behaviour-based on purpose: user agents are spoofable, so they are enrichment only. Feeds PB3 (enrich + block).
# Thresholds are starting guesses: >= 5 distinct blocking rules, or >= 300 requests over >= 60 distinct paths.
fields httpRequest.clientIp as ip, httpRequest.country as country, httpRequest.uri as uri, action, terminatingRuleId
| parse @message '"terminatingRule":{"ruleId":"*"' as managedRuleId
| fields coalesce(managedRuleId, terminatingRuleId) as rule
| stats count(*) as requests,
        countDistinct(uri) as paths,
        countDistinct(rule) as rulesHit,
        latest(action) as lastAction
        by ip, country, bin(10m)
| filter rulesHit >= 5 or (requests >= 300 and paths >= 60)
| sort rulesHit desc
| limit 200
